From b9f6d31c219e1ccdfdb21cee1656565f0cac7dad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pablo Dorado <pablo@bloque.team>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:54:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(kernel): refuse an entry whose ledger differs from
 its account's

The zero-sum invariant groups entries by their own `(ledger, layer)`,
and nothing compared `entry.ledger` with the ledger of the account the
entry posts to. A transfer could label both legs USD while crediting a
EUR account: the (USD, Settled) group balances, the kernel accepts it,
and value crosses currencies at a rate nobody signed.

After loading the touched accounts, the kernel now checks every entry's
`ledger` against its account's and refuses a mismatch with the new
`EventStatus::EntryLedgerMustMatchAccount` (44, in the cross-field
consistency block). `TransferBuilder` already copies `account.ledger`
into each entry, so builder-made transfers are unaffected; the check
catches hand-built entries. The shadow model in `proptest_shadow`
mirrors the check.

Tests: `tests/kernel_entry_currency.rs` (mismatch on the credit leg,
on the debit leg, the matching case, and the builder case).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
